select - wait for file descriptor readiness

SYNOPSIS
    #include <sys/select.h>

    int select(int nfds, fd_set *readfds, fd_set *writefds,
        fd_set *exceptfds, struct timeval *timeout);

DESCRIPTION
    Test descriptors smaller than nfds for readiness. Build sets
    with FD_ZERO, FD_SET and FD_CLR. On return, FD_ISSET reports
    which requested descriptors are ready.

    Regular files, pipes, the console, and input devices can be
    selected. A null timeout waits for an event or a signal.
    A zero timeout checks readiness immediately. A positive
    timeout is rounded up to the system clock quantum.

    Project9 clears exceptfds. No device reports exceptional
    conditions through this set.

RETURN VALUES
    The result is the number of ready bits, zero on timeout,
    or -1 on error. A caught signal can cause EINTR.

SEE ALSO
    mmap(2), dev(5)
